FFmpeg
======

The libraries avcodec, avformat, avutil, swresample and swscale in this jar
are FFmpeg @FFMPEG_VERSION@ (https://ffmpeg.org), licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License version 2.1 or later. The full text of that license is in
COPYING.LGPLv2.1, next to this file.

They are built without --enable-gpl and without --enable-nonfree, so no part
of them is under the GPL or a non-free license.

They are linked dynamically: the webrtc-java-media library loads them as
separate shared libraries, which you may replace with your own build of a
compatible FFmpeg version.


Source code
-----------

The libraries are built from the FFmpeg release n@FFMPEG_VERSION@, without
modifications:

  https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n@FFMPEG_VERSION@
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-@FFMPEG_VERSION@.tar.xz

How they are configured and built, including which demuxers, decoders,
parsers and protocols are enabled, is set out in
webrtc-java-media/src/main/cpp/dependencies/ffmpeg/CMakeLists.txt of
webrtc-java, at the release this jar belongs to:

  https://github.com/devopvoid/webrtc-java


Patents
-------

Some of the formats FFmpeg decodes, such as H.264, H.265/HEVC and AAC, may be
covered by patents in some countries. Whether your use of them needs a patent
license is for you to determine.
